Test vectors for vlpds's Spaces primitives (src/space), from the reference
implementation:

  repo:   https://github.com/bluesky-social/atproto
  branch: permissioned-data (PR #5187)
  commit: 98ef3a6b9d1364f0543f137dd024de9651b21c4c

vectors.json was generated, not copied: the reference's own tests use
random keys and check round trips. gen-vectors.mjs produced it by running the
reference code (@atproto/space at that commit, built in the harness's
reference image, bench/spaces/refpds.sh; see its header) with fixed keys and
shared secrets: the LtHash, the KEM shared secret (the repo host's side), the
commit and record MACs and their headers, STAR archives (serializeRepo,
serializeSpaceMeta), HTTP message signatures and tokens. Each vector was
verified by the reference before it was written out. Only the token jtis are
random, so a re-run changes the `tokens` entries alone.

star-interop/ holds the DASL STAR interop fixtures, copied unmodified (their
README names the upstream commit and license); src/space/star.rs reads every
one.

HTTP signature, token and MAC cases (src/space/{httpsig,token,commit,mac}.rs
tests) are ported from packages/space/src/http-signature.test.ts,
packages/space/tests/credential.test.ts, mac.test.ts and kem.test.ts, at the
same commit. Syntax cases (src/lexicon.rs tests) are ported from
packages/syntax/tests/aturi-string.test.ts and
packages/lexicon/tests/general.test.ts.

License: MIT (bluesky-social/atproto).

export.star and export.json (tests/all/spaces_side/import_repo.rs) are a space
repo as the reference PDS's com.atproto.space.getRepo serves it, generated by
gen-export.mjs at the same commit: the reference's serializeRecord,
RepoCommit.toCommit and serializeRepo over five records (one naming a blob),
checked with readRepoStar before it was written. STAR carries nothing random,
so a re-run gives the same bytes.
